        "original_id": "37323971-7c0e-53d4-8ffe-dce337dc726b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Charles Spitzka, Charles Guiteau, James A. Garfield\n- Roles: neurologist, medical specialist in mental diseases, President of the United States\n- Events: Guiteau's murder trial, assassination of James A. Garfield\n\nFacts:\n- James A. Garfield was born on November 19, 1831.\n- On March 4, 1881, James A. Garfield began serving as the 20th President of the United States.\n- In 1881, Edward Charles Spitzka, a neurologist and medical specialist in mental diseases, testified that Charles Guiteau was insane at Guiteau's murder trial.\n- James A. Garfield was assassinated in 1881.\n- James A. Garfield died on September 19, 1881, after serving as president until his assassination that year.",
